WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.300
♪

00:07.300 --> 00:08.300
Opie!

00:09.200 --> 00:11.600
What in the world happened? Who did that to you?

00:11.600 --> 00:13.400
Matt Merlis. He's my best friend.

00:13.400 --> 00:16.900
I hate to think what you do is your enemy.

00:16.900 --> 00:18.600
You're a sight.

00:18.600 --> 00:21.500
You better get home, let Aunt Bee clean you up and fix your britches.

00:21.500 --> 00:24.500
She ain't home. Miss Clara's sick and she went over to help out.

00:24.500 --> 00:25.500
Oh.

00:25.500 --> 00:26.500
Phew!

00:27.100 --> 00:28.500
I better do something.

00:28.500 --> 00:30.500
Mmm.

00:30.500 --> 00:31.500
Come on.

00:34.000 --> 00:37.500
I suppose you tell me how you got yourself all messed up like that.

00:39.000 --> 00:40.000
Look at that.

00:40.000 --> 00:42.000
You gonna put that stuff on? It stings.

00:42.000 --> 00:43.000
Mmm.

00:43.000 --> 00:45.000
Just antiseptic salt.

00:47.000 --> 00:48.000
There we are.

00:51.000 --> 00:53.000
Yeah. There we are.

00:53.500 --> 00:54.500
Stop it!

00:55.500 --> 00:57.000
I ain't touched you yet.

00:57.000 --> 00:59.000
What happens if you don't put it on?

00:59.000 --> 01:00.000
Do I die?

01:00.000 --> 01:05.000
No, but your knee might get infected and then you'd have to go to Doc Harvey's and get a shot.

01:06.000 --> 01:08.000
I'll take the antiseptic.

01:10.000 --> 01:11.000
Andy?

01:11.000 --> 01:12.000
Back here, Barn.

01:13.000 --> 01:15.000
Now, boo, you tell me what happened.

01:15.000 --> 01:18.000
Some of us got into a rough house on the playground.

01:18.000 --> 01:19.000
A fight?

01:20.000 --> 01:23.000
No, it was just wrestling. Having fun.

01:23.000 --> 01:28.000
You young'uns sure have fun the hard way, don't you? There you are.

01:28.000 --> 01:29.000
Thanks, Pa.

01:29.000 --> 01:30.000
No, wait a minute.

01:31.000 --> 01:32.000
Well.

01:33.000 --> 01:34.000
One more time.

01:35.000 --> 01:36.000
Alright.

01:36.000 --> 01:40.000
Now, suppose you go on home and get that wash rag you hate so much and get cleaned up.

01:40.000 --> 01:41.000
Thank you, Pa.

01:41.000 --> 01:42.000
Okay, go on.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.000
Pa?

01:45.000 --> 01:46.000
What?

01:46.000 --> 01:49.000
You got to come to school and see my teacher.

01:49.000 --> 01:50.000
How's that?

01:50.000 --> 01:56.000
Miss Crump saw us all scrambling around on the playground and she said she wanted to see the mothers of all the boys it was fighting.

01:56.000 --> 01:59.000
So, Pa, I guess you're going to have to go for me.

01:59.000 --> 02:01.000
Alright, I'll try to get over there sometime tomorrow.

02:01.000 --> 02:13.000
Young'uns, young'uns, young'uns, young'uns, young'uns.

02:31.000 --> 02:33.000
What were you going to talk to me about?

02:34.000 --> 02:36.000
Trouble between you and Thumbeloo?

02:38.000 --> 02:40.000
What were you going to talk to me about?

02:42.000 --> 02:43.000
You.

02:44.000 --> 02:45.000
Me?

02:46.000 --> 02:48.000
Well, what were you going to talk to me about?

02:50.000 --> 02:53.000
How long do you think you can do it?

02:53.000 --> 02:54.000
Do what?

02:54.000 --> 02:59.000
How long do you think you can be father and mother to that boy?

02:59.000 --> 03:05.000
Now, Andy, you owe it to Opie and just as important, if not more so, you owe it to yourself.

03:05.000 --> 03:07.000
You ain't going to start that again, are you?

03:07.000 --> 03:08.000
Start it for what again?

03:08.000 --> 03:12.000
Start talking about why don't I get married, because I don't want to talk about that.

03:12.000 --> 03:13.000
Okay.

03:14.000 --> 03:17.000
You don't want to talk about it, we won't talk about it.

03:17.000 --> 03:29.000
I appreciate it.

03:29.000 --> 03:33.000
You know what they say about a man that keeps putting off getting married?

03:36.000 --> 03:38.000
They say he starts getting irritable.

03:40.000 --> 03:42.000
Well, that's what they say.

03:42.000 --> 03:45.000
Especially a man that's been married once before.

03:46.000 --> 03:51.000
He knows he's going to have to take the plunge again someday, but he keeps putting it off.

03:52.000 --> 04:00.000
And the more he keeps putting it off, the more desperate he gets, and the more desperate he gets, the more irritable he gets, and the more...

04:00.000 --> 04:01.000
Will you shut up?

04:01.000 --> 04:03.000
There, you see how irritable you are? It proves my point.

04:03.000 --> 04:07.000
It proves you're worrying me to death while I'm trying to work. That's what it proves.

04:07.000 --> 04:11.000
It proves you're worrying me to death while I'm trying to work. That's what it proves.

04:14.000 --> 04:16.000
You want me to tell you? I'll tell you.

04:17.000 --> 04:20.000
I ain't found the woman I want to marry yet.

04:20.000 --> 04:21.000
I ain't putting it off.

04:21.000 --> 04:23.000
I miss being married.

04:23.000 --> 04:25.000
Sometimes I get to feeling downright lonesome.

04:25.000 --> 04:27.000
I miss going home to a wife.

04:27.000 --> 04:33.000
But then, you see, getting married means you found the woman you want to settle down with, and I ain't found her yet.

04:33.000 --> 04:36.000
But when I do, you'll be the first to know, okay?

04:36.000 --> 04:42.000
Do you mean to tell me that in all of Mayberry, there ain't one woman for you?

04:42.000 --> 04:46.000
I didn't say that. I didn't say that at all.

04:47.000 --> 04:50.000
She might very well be here. I just ain't found her yet.

04:50.000 --> 04:54.000
But till I do, the subject is closed, right?

04:54.000 --> 04:56.000
Oh, closed tight, buddy.

04:57.000 --> 04:58.000
Good.

04:58.000 --> 05:03.000
As long as I made my point with you, the subject is closed and put away.

05:03.000 --> 05:05.000
That's fine.

05:08.000 --> 05:11.000
You know what my point was, is you owe it to yourself, you know.

05:11.000 --> 05:12.000
Barney!

05:12.000 --> 05:13.000
Oh!

05:14.000 --> 05:17.000
All right. Let's see.

05:17.000 --> 05:19.000
Well, I'm going now. I won't be long.

05:19.000 --> 05:22.000
I'm just bringing Clara something over for supper.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.000
You know that poor dear can hardly get around.

05:24.000 --> 05:26.000
Well, what's the matter with her anyway?

05:26.000 --> 05:30.000
Well, she spilled some bacon grease behind the stove, and she was afraid it would attract ants.

05:30.000 --> 05:35.000
So she tried to lift the stove to clean it up, and now she's walking crooked.

05:35.000 --> 05:37.000
Oh!

05:37.000 --> 05:39.000
Well, you give her my best.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.000
I will.

05:40.000 --> 05:42.000
Opie, one story, enough to bed.

05:42.000 --> 05:44.000
Okay. A.B.?

05:44.000 --> 05:45.000
Hmm?

05:45.000 --> 05:49.000
If Miss Clara gets ants, tell her not to kill them. I'll bring them home and make an ant farm.

05:49.000 --> 05:51.000
Oh, no, you won't.

05:51.000 --> 05:52.000
Good night.

05:53.000 --> 05:55.000
All right. Now, Opie, what story will it be?

05:56.000 --> 05:59.000
The Headless Horseman. That's my favorite.

05:59.000 --> 06:02.000
Mm-hmm. Legend of Sleepy Hollow. All right. There we are.

06:02.000 --> 06:04.000
You ought to know this in my heart by now.

06:06.000 --> 06:13.000
It was the very witching time of night that Ichabod, heavy-hearted and crestfallen, pursued his travel homeward,

06:13.000 --> 06:17.000
along the sides of the lofty hills which rise above Tarrytown,

06:17.000 --> 06:20.000
and which he had traversed so cheerily in the afternoon.

06:20.000 --> 06:27.000
I wonder who that is. Don't lose the place.

06:31.000 --> 06:32.000
Hello, Andy.

06:32.000 --> 06:36.000
Oh, hi, Amanda. How are you? I haven't seen you in a long time.

06:36.000 --> 06:38.000
Oh, it has been some time.

06:39.000 --> 06:41.000
What brings you out this way?

06:41.000 --> 06:46.000
Oh, well, I got a message saying I was to meet Thelma Lou here. Isn't she here?

06:46.000 --> 06:53.000
Oh, no, she's not. But if she said for you to meet her out here, I expect she'll be along. Won't you come on in?

06:53.000 --> 06:55.000
I hope I'm not interrupting anything.

06:55.000 --> 06:58.000
Oh, no. I was just reading Opie's story.

06:58.000 --> 07:03.000
Oh, please don't let me stop you. I'll just sit right over here. You go right ahead.

07:03.000 --> 07:05.000
All right. You just excuse us.

07:06.000 --> 07:12.000
It was the very witching time of night that Ichabod, heavy-hearted and crestfallen, pursued his travel homeward,

07:12.000 --> 07:21.000
along the sides of the lofty hills which rise above Tarrytown, and which he had traversed so cheerily in the afternoon.

07:23.000 --> 07:25.000
Oh, maybe that's Thelma Lou now.

07:29.000 --> 07:30.000
Hi, Andy.

07:31.000 --> 07:34.000
Oh, hi, Lavinia. This is a surprise. How have you been?

07:34.000 --> 07:38.000
Fine. I'm supposed to meet Thelma Lou here.

07:38.000 --> 07:42.000
Oh. Well, Amanda's here waiting for her, too. Won't you come in?

07:42.000 --> 07:48.000
She is? Well, hi, Amanda. Hi, Lavinia.

07:48.000 --> 07:50.000
Oh, come sit down.

07:50.000 --> 07:55.000
Now, Andy, you just read your story, and we'll talk very quietly and try not to disturb you.

07:55.000 --> 07:56.000
Excuse us.

07:56.000 --> 07:58.000
Let me keep in. I haven't seen you in such a long time.

07:58.000 --> 08:02.000
It was the very witching time of night that Ichabod, heavy-hearted and crestfallen,

08:02.000 --> 08:08.000
pursued his travels homeward, along the sides of the lofty hills which rise above Tarrytown,

08:08.000 --> 08:11.000
and which he had traversed so cheerily in the afternoon.

08:14.000 --> 08:15.000
I hope that's Thelma Lou.

08:21.000 --> 08:23.000
Hi, Rosemary. Blanche.

08:23.000 --> 08:25.000
Hello. We're here to meet Thelma Lou.

08:25.000 --> 08:29.000
You're here to meet Thelma Lou. Won't you come on in? There's some others waiting for her.

08:29.000 --> 08:32.000
Well, hi, Lavinia. Hi, Amanda.

08:32.000 --> 08:35.000
Oh, it's so good to have a seat with you.

08:35.000 --> 08:36.000
Oh, get up.

08:36.000 --> 08:41.000
Ladies, if you all will excuse us, I was just reading my boy a story.

08:41.000 --> 08:43.000
You just make yourself at home.

08:43.000 --> 08:45.000
Oh, is that right?

08:45.000 --> 08:47.000
I may not have one.

08:48.000 --> 08:51.000
How come Thelma Lou asked all them girls to meet her here?

08:52.000 --> 08:53.000
I don't know.

08:53.000 --> 08:56.000
Maybe they're painting over her house, and that makes a mess,

08:56.000 --> 08:59.000
or so she just didn't like them over here.

09:00.000 --> 09:03.000
It was the very witching time of night that Ichabod...

09:08.000 --> 09:12.000
Maybe we better read this story another time. They're starting to pile up now.

09:12.000 --> 09:15.000
I'm going up to bed, and I'll be up at five.

09:15.000 --> 09:16.000
Okay, Pa. Night.

09:16.000 --> 09:17.000
Night.

09:17.000 --> 09:20.000
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa. I didn't mean to.

09:20.000 --> 09:23.000
No, he's not likeable. He is not likeable.

09:23.000 --> 09:24.000
I don't blame him.

09:24.000 --> 09:47.000
Good evening, ladies. If you're here to meet Thelma Lou, come right on in.

09:55.000 --> 09:57.000
Oh, my God.

10:08.000 --> 10:09.000
Girls!

10:10.000 --> 10:13.000
Ladies, ladies, I don't...

10:14.000 --> 10:20.000
Ladies, ladies, I don't know why Thelma Lou's not here yet.

10:20.000 --> 10:23.000
I'll get on the phone and call her.

10:27.000 --> 10:29.000
Excuse me, that's the back door.

10:38.000 --> 10:40.000
Now, here, what do you think?

10:40.000 --> 10:41.000
What?

10:41.000 --> 10:44.000
The girls. Any prospects? See anything you like?

10:44.000 --> 10:47.000
You don't mean to tell me you sent them girls over here?

10:47.000 --> 10:49.000
See, this way you get to see them all at once.

10:49.000 --> 10:54.000
You check off what you like, and if you don't see anything you like, we send in another batch tomorrow night.

10:56.000 --> 10:58.000
Listen to them out there.

10:58.000 --> 11:01.000
Just think, one of them might be the next Mrs. Annie Taylor.

11:01.000 --> 11:03.000
Right behind that door. Don't that excite you?

11:03.000 --> 11:05.000
Get them girls out of here.

11:05.000 --> 11:06.000
What's wrong?

11:06.000 --> 11:08.000
Get them girls out of here.

11:08.000 --> 11:10.000
Well, what's the matter? They don't know why they're here.

11:10.000 --> 11:14.000
You just look them over, and you say, this one is out, this one's a maybe, this one's a...

11:14.000 --> 11:17.000
Get them girls out of here.

11:17.000 --> 11:18.000
Okay.

11:18.000 --> 11:19.000
Okay?

11:19.000 --> 11:21.000
You're right, yeah.

11:21.000 --> 11:24.000
I see what you mean. You see too many one time, you get confused.

11:24.000 --> 11:25.000
Get them right out.

11:25.000 --> 11:26.000
Barney.

11:27.000 --> 11:29.000
Why are you doing all this for me?

11:30.000 --> 11:31.000
Why?

11:32.000 --> 11:34.000
You crazy guy.

11:34.000 --> 11:36.000
Even asking such a thing.

11:36.000 --> 11:39.000
Because I'm your best friend, I want to make you happy.

11:40.000 --> 11:41.000
Crazy guy.

11:43.000 --> 11:45.000
All right, girls.

11:45.000 --> 11:46.000
All right, girls.

11:47.000 --> 11:48.000
Girls.

11:48.000 --> 11:49.000
Girls.

11:57.000 --> 12:01.000
Now girls, you're probably wondering why you're all asked here this evening.

12:01.000 --> 12:02.000
We did.

12:02.000 --> 12:09.000
Well, I asked you here on behalf of Thelma Lou, who is going to speak to you on a subject of interest to you all.

12:09.000 --> 12:14.000
But now Thelma Lou can't make it, so the meeting has been postponed.

12:14.000 --> 12:22.000
Now I'll let you know the time and the place of the next meeting, and in the meantime, thanks a lot for this swell turnout.

12:22.000 --> 12:23.000
What turnout?

12:23.000 --> 12:25.000
What did we turn out for?

12:32.000 --> 12:34.000
I wish I knew what this was all about.

12:34.000 --> 12:35.000
I do too.

12:35.000 --> 12:36.000
Stupid I am.

12:36.000 --> 12:39.000
Are you sure you don't see one of these girls you like? They're all hand-picked, you know.

12:39.000 --> 12:40.000
Party horn.

12:41.000 --> 12:44.000
Oh, well, it's just a big mystery, the whole thing.

12:45.000 --> 12:47.000
Well, the search goes on.

12:57.000 --> 12:58.000
Hi, Thelma Lou.

12:58.000 --> 12:59.000
Hi, Lorraine.

13:01.000 --> 13:02.000
Who's that?

13:02.000 --> 13:03.000
Lorraine Beasley.

13:03.000 --> 13:05.000
Lorraine Beasley?

13:06.000 --> 13:10.000
Well, she might be a little young for Andy, but she's a possum.

13:10.000 --> 13:13.000
You're not really serious about this, are you?

13:13.000 --> 13:15.000
Well, of course I am.

13:15.000 --> 13:19.000
Making up a list of girls that might be right for Andy, it's just...

13:19.000 --> 13:20.000
It's just what?

13:21.000 --> 13:23.000
Well, you don't find a wife that way.

13:23.000 --> 13:26.000
That's what you do when you're trying to organize a girl's softball team.

13:26.000 --> 13:29.000
These are only suggestions, is all.

13:29.000 --> 13:31.000
Why not leave that for me?

13:31.000 --> 13:33.000
Because he wouldn't do nothing about it.

13:33.000 --> 13:35.000
Thelma Lou, Andy's a lonely man.

13:35.000 --> 13:37.000
Hi, Annabelle.

13:39.000 --> 13:40.000
Annabelle who?

13:41.000 --> 13:42.000
She's married.

13:49.000 --> 13:50.000
Wait a minute.

13:50.000 --> 13:52.000
Well, boys are going to roughhouse.

13:52.000 --> 13:54.000
I just don't want them to get themselves hurt.

13:54.000 --> 13:58.000
Well, I hope he won't be giving you any more trouble for a while, anyway.

13:58.000 --> 13:59.000
Of course.

13:59.000 --> 14:02.000
She's the most logical candidate of all.

14:02.000 --> 14:03.000
Opie's teacher.

14:03.000 --> 14:04.000
What?

14:04.000 --> 14:05.000
What are you looking at?

14:06.000 --> 14:09.000
Maybe the future Mrs. Andy Taylor is all.

14:09.000 --> 14:12.000
And you and I are going to help it along, sweetie.

14:12.000 --> 14:15.000
The first thing we do is plan a little dinner.

14:17.000 --> 14:18.000
Well, thank you, Thelma Lou.

14:18.000 --> 14:19.000
That's nice of you.

14:20.000 --> 14:21.000
About seven?

14:22.000 --> 14:23.000
Fine, I'll be there.

14:25.000 --> 14:26.000
Much obliged.

14:26.000 --> 14:28.000
Much obliged.

14:32.000 --> 14:33.000
That's nice of her.

14:33.000 --> 14:34.000
Mm-hmm.

14:41.000 --> 14:42.000
Wait a minute.

14:44.000 --> 14:46.000
What do you know about this?

14:47.000 --> 14:48.000
Huh?

14:49.000 --> 14:51.000
Thelma Lou invited me to dinner.

14:51.000 --> 14:52.000
What's the occasion?

14:52.000 --> 14:55.000
Uh, no occasion.

14:55.000 --> 15:00.000
She was just saying the other day how she hadn't had you to dinner in a long time.

15:00.000 --> 15:03.000
Thelma Lou ain't ever had me to dinner.

15:03.000 --> 15:05.000
Well, there you are.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.000
It hasn't been a long time.

15:16.000 --> 15:17.000
Andy!

15:19.000 --> 15:20.000
Oh, come here.

15:20.000 --> 15:22.000
Thelma, Andy Lou's here!

15:26.000 --> 15:27.000
See ya.

15:29.000 --> 15:30.000
What's the matter with you?

15:30.000 --> 15:32.000
Oh, me? Nothing. I'm just glad to see ya.

15:33.000 --> 15:35.000
Must be. You're still shaking my hand.

15:36.000 --> 15:38.000
Oh, well. Come on in.

15:39.000 --> 15:41.000
I believe you two know each other.

15:43.000 --> 15:44.000
Good evening.

15:46.000 --> 15:48.000
Well, this is a surprise.

15:48.000 --> 15:50.000
Yeah, it is a surprise, isn't it?

15:50.000 --> 15:52.000
That's what I thought you'd say, that it was a surprise.

15:53.000 --> 15:54.000
Hi, Andy.

15:54.000 --> 15:55.000
Oh, hi.

15:55.000 --> 15:58.000
Thelma Lou, you know what Andy said when he saw Miss Crump sitting there?

15:58.000 --> 16:00.000
He said it was a surprise.

16:00.000 --> 16:01.000
Oh, really?

16:01.000 --> 16:03.000
Yeah, he just walked in, took one look and...

16:03.000 --> 16:06.000
How'd you say that, Andy? Say it for Thelma Lou.

16:08.000 --> 16:10.000
I just said that it was a surprise.

16:10.000 --> 16:12.000
That's just the way he said it.

16:12.000 --> 16:14.000
You were surprised, weren't ya?

16:14.000 --> 16:17.000
Yeah, but I'm not anymore.

16:17.000 --> 16:20.000
You know, I hardly recognized you without your uniform.

16:20.000 --> 16:23.000
Yeah, he does look different, don't he? I think he looks taller.

16:23.000 --> 16:26.000
Don't you, Thelma Lou, don't you think Andy looks taller when he's in his uniform?

16:26.000 --> 16:27.000
Come on, Barney.

16:27.000 --> 16:28.000
Well, you do. You look taller.

16:28.000 --> 16:32.000
Miss Crump, why don't you just stand up there alongside Andy and see if you don't look taller.

16:32.000 --> 16:33.000
Barney, uh...

16:33.000 --> 16:35.000
Go on. Go on. Just stand there alongside of him.

16:37.000 --> 16:38.000
There, you see?

16:38.000 --> 16:40.000
I believe you're right.

16:40.000 --> 16:43.000
They look great together. Just great.

16:43.000 --> 16:47.000
Well, I hope you aren't all starved. Dinner won't be for a little while yet.

16:47.000 --> 16:51.000
Well, what's the hurry? We want to talk a little while anyway, don't we?

16:51.000 --> 16:53.000
Why don't we just sit down?

16:53.000 --> 16:55.000
Go on. Just have a seat.

16:56.000 --> 16:58.000
There we go.

17:00.000 --> 17:03.000
Dinner certainly does smell wonderful, whatever it is.

17:03.000 --> 17:05.000
Oh, it's just leg of lamb.

17:05.000 --> 17:08.000
Leg of lamb? Good, good.

17:08.000 --> 17:10.000
That's my favorite dish.

17:11.000 --> 17:14.000
Did you hear that, Miss Crump? That's Andy's favorite dish.

17:15.000 --> 17:19.000
Son of a gun. Ever since I can remember, it's been his favorite dish.

17:19.000 --> 17:22.000
I bet you cook a mean leg of lamb yourself, don't you?

17:22.000 --> 17:24.000
Goodness, no. I wouldn't even know where to start.

17:24.000 --> 17:26.000
Oh, come on.

17:26.000 --> 17:27.000
No, really.

17:28.000 --> 17:32.000
You mean you don't know how to cook leg of lamb? Andy's favorite dish?

17:32.000 --> 17:34.000
No, as a matter of fact, I'm a terrible cook.

17:34.000 --> 17:38.000
You're just saying that. You're being modest.

17:39.000 --> 17:44.000
Barney, Miss Crump's so busy teaching all day, she don't have time to fool with cooking.

17:44.000 --> 17:46.000
Oh, yeah, I suppose that's true.

17:46.000 --> 17:50.000
But then someday when you settle down, I mean when you get married or something like that,

17:50.000 --> 17:54.000
well, you'll probably start to cook and then you'll just make a terrific leg of lamb.

17:54.000 --> 17:56.000
Andy's favorite dish.

17:56.000 --> 17:58.000
I really doubt it.

17:58.000 --> 18:00.000
Well, holy cats, why don't you feed your husband?

18:00.000 --> 18:02.000
I mean, if you get married or something.

18:02.000 --> 18:05.000
Well, I suppose he'll just have to settle for frozen dinners.

18:05.000 --> 18:07.000
You're kidding.

18:07.000 --> 18:11.000
What's wrong with frozen dinners, Bar? They're good. I like them.

18:11.000 --> 18:12.000
No, you don't.

18:12.000 --> 18:16.000
You're going to be home all day. Well, then you'll have lots of time.

18:16.000 --> 18:19.000
Ah, but I won't be home all day. I'll still be teaching, I hope.

18:19.000 --> 18:22.000
You mean you're not going to give up your job when you get married?

18:22.000 --> 18:24.000
Well, I hope not. I enjoy teaching.

18:24.000 --> 18:28.000
Women don't do that anymore, Barney. This is the 20th century.

18:28.000 --> 18:29.000
I know what century it is.

18:29.000 --> 18:32.000
Don't you think we'd better start getting that dinner on?

18:32.000 --> 18:34.000
I don't think it's ready yet, Barney.

18:34.000 --> 18:37.000
Well, let's just check on that. Excuse us.

18:45.000 --> 18:47.000
The sooner we get this over with, the better.

18:47.000 --> 18:48.000
Barney, why?

18:48.000 --> 18:50.000
Because I made a mistake, that's why.

18:50.000 --> 18:52.000
This day means for Andy, now we cross her off our list.

18:52.000 --> 18:53.000
But why?

18:53.000 --> 18:55.000
Because she can't cook. She can't do nothing.

18:55.000 --> 18:56.000
Barney.

18:56.000 --> 18:59.000
Now she's out. O-U-T, out. Now get the dinner up.

18:59.000 --> 19:00.000
But I don't think it's ready yet.

19:00.000 --> 19:02.000
Ready or not, let's get it over with and get on to the next one.

19:02.000 --> 19:04.000
Okay, folks, dinner.

19:11.000 --> 19:13.000
Andy, listen. I just want...

19:13.000 --> 19:14.000
Wait a minute.

19:16.000 --> 19:17.000
Thanks, buddy.

19:17.000 --> 19:18.000
Huh?

19:18.000 --> 19:21.000
For last night. I really enjoyed it.

19:21.000 --> 19:23.000
Helen's one of the nicest girls I ever met.

19:23.000 --> 19:25.000
Helen?

19:25.000 --> 19:26.000
Miss Crump.

19:26.000 --> 19:27.000
It's Helen?

19:27.000 --> 19:28.000
Yeah.

19:28.000 --> 19:31.000
After Thelma Luz, I walked her home and got better acquainted.

19:31.000 --> 19:32.000
Nice girl.

19:32.000 --> 19:34.000
And I owe it all to you.

19:34.000 --> 19:36.000
Helen?

19:36.000 --> 19:37.000
Yeah.

19:38.000 --> 19:40.000
She's not for you, Andy.

19:40.000 --> 19:41.000
What?

19:41.000 --> 19:42.000
She's not for you.

19:42.000 --> 19:45.000
Now just forget it. Forget last night.

19:45.000 --> 19:46.000
What are you talking about?

19:46.000 --> 19:48.000
Last night was the first of many experiments.

19:48.000 --> 19:51.000
Now it failed, so just forget it.

19:51.000 --> 19:53.000
Well, why should I? I like her.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.000
No, you don't. No. Just forget it.

19:55.000 --> 19:57.000
That's what I do.

19:57.000 --> 19:59.000
She's pleasant. She's interested. I enjoy her company.

19:59.000 --> 20:03.000
Andy, I forbid you to see that girl again.

20:03.000 --> 20:05.000
Are you out of your mind?

20:05.000 --> 20:08.000
I got a date for tonight. She's coming to dinner.

20:08.000 --> 20:09.000
Andy!

20:09.000 --> 20:10.000
Forget it!

20:15.000 --> 20:16.000
Coming!

20:21.000 --> 20:22.000
Hello, Andy.

20:22.000 --> 20:24.000
Hi, Amanda. Don't tell me that...

20:24.000 --> 20:25.000
Well, here we go again.

20:25.000 --> 20:27.000
I got a call saying to meet Thelma Luz here.

20:27.000 --> 20:28.000
She get here yet?

20:28.000 --> 20:29.000
Uh, no.

20:29.000 --> 20:31.000
Now, don't you let me interrupt anything.

20:31.000 --> 20:33.000
You just go right ahead with whatever you were doing.

20:33.000 --> 20:34.000
Well, all right.

20:40.000 --> 20:42.000
Hi, Andy. Thelma Luz here yet?

20:42.000 --> 20:46.000
Uh, Lavinia, I don't... I don't think that Thelma Luz actually...

20:46.000 --> 20:47.000
I know.

20:47.000 --> 20:49.000
Oh, my God.

20:51.000 --> 20:53.000
I don't know why.

21:03.000 --> 21:05.000
What's this all about?

21:07.000 --> 21:09.000
I'm sorry, Andy, but I had to do it.

21:09.000 --> 21:11.000
You'll thank me for it someday.

21:11.000 --> 21:13.000
I know it was a rotten thing to do, but I had to do it.

21:13.000 --> 21:14.000
What?

21:14.000 --> 21:16.000
Has Miss Crump been here and took off?

21:16.000 --> 21:17.000
No.

21:18.000 --> 21:19.000
Oh.

21:19.000 --> 21:22.000
Well, when she does get here and sees all them girls, she will.

21:22.000 --> 21:25.000
She'll get the idea you got a lot of girlfriends and she'll leave.

21:25.000 --> 21:27.000
You do have a dinner date this evening.

21:27.000 --> 21:28.000
Yeah.

21:28.000 --> 21:31.000
I'm gonna pick her up at her house and take her to Mount Pilot for Chinese.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.000
You wanna come in here?

21:37.000 --> 21:41.000
Girls, girls, girls, you wanna... Quiet down, girls.

21:41.000 --> 21:44.000
Girls, girls, you wanna... Quiet down.

21:44.000 --> 21:47.000
You're probably all wondering why you was asked here this evening.

21:47.000 --> 21:48.000
We sure are.

21:48.000 --> 21:51.000
Well, I don't have any idea.

21:51.000 --> 21:54.000
But Deputy Pipe, who called you, might.

21:54.000 --> 21:56.000
Tell him, Barney.

22:00.000 --> 22:02.000
What is this, Barney?

22:02.000 --> 22:04.000
Yes, it's the second time now.

22:04.000 --> 22:06.000
Listen, we wanna know what's going on here.

22:06.000 --> 22:07.000
Quiet, girls.

22:07.000 --> 22:09.000
Girls, just a minute, girls.

22:09.000 --> 22:14.000
Uh, have you girls ever thought of starting a softball team?

22:31.000 --> 22:32.000
Andy?

22:32.000 --> 22:38.000
Barney?

22:38.000 --> 22:40.000
Uh, Andy?

22:41.000 --> 22:43.000
Barney?

22:44.000 --> 22:49.000
Uh, I got something I wanna say and I want you to hear me out.

22:53.000 --> 22:57.000
I've been meddling too much in your personal affairs.

22:57.000 --> 22:59.000
Oh, now, I...

22:59.000 --> 23:04.000
Please, please, now, I've been meddling too much in your personal affairs and...

23:04.000 --> 23:07.000
Well, the time's come for me to stop it.

23:07.000 --> 23:10.000
After all, you're a grown man and...

23:10.000 --> 23:14.000
certainly don't need the likes of me to advise you or to guide you or...

23:14.000 --> 23:17.000
tell you who to go with or who not to go with.

23:17.000 --> 23:22.000
It's your life and yours to do whatever you please with it.

23:22.000 --> 23:27.000
And whoever you wanna marry, well, that's your own business.

23:27.000 --> 23:30.000
And I just ain't gonna interfere.

23:31.000 --> 23:34.000
And that's all I had to say.

23:38.000 --> 23:41.000
Well, I appreciate that, Barney.

23:41.000 --> 23:44.000
And I'm glad you feel that way.

23:45.000 --> 23:48.000
Because I've got something I wanna tell you too.

23:50.000 --> 23:53.000
I've decided I'm gonna court Miss Crump.

23:53.000 --> 23:55.000
Miss Crump?

23:55.000 --> 23:57.000
Are you kidding, Andy?

23:57.000 --> 23:59.000
Well, she can't even cook a leg of lamb!

23:59.000 --> 24:26.000
She said herself she's a terrible cook!

